# npm run dev/build/start explicitly use local preview accounts and synthetic reporting data.
# Real authentication is only used by build:production/start:production.
# Configure these server-side for production authentication:
# AUTH_URL=https://dashboard.example.com
# DYNAMODB_REGION=us-east-2
# DYNAMODB_USERS_TABLE=
# DYNAMODB_WHITELIST_TABLE=
# DASHBOARD_AUTH_SECRET_ARN=arn:aws:secretsmanager:us-east-2:123456789012:secret:dashboard-auth-xxxxxx
# Managed Amplify builds require the fields above. Only these non-secret settings
# enter the server artifact; the signing key is fetched at runtime with the SSR IAM role.
# SecretString may be raw text or JSON {"authSecret":"at least 32 random characters"}.
# Direct local production runs may instead supply AUTH_SECRET at runtime (never at build).
# Do not add signing keys or AWS credentials to next.config env or public settings.
